# Triangular prism for the chromatic-dispersion demo preset.
# Authored in standard Y-up convention (Y=height, X=width, Z=depth) --
# the engine's model-loading pipeline bakes a +90 deg X rotation that converts
# this to its own Z-up world convention, and a +180 deg Y rotation.
# Cross-section (in the XY plane): apex at (0, 0.87), base at (-0.5,0)/(0.5,0),
# roughly equilateral (side length 1.0). Extruded along Z from -0.75 to 0.75.
mtllib prism.mtl
usemtl glass

v 0.0 0.87 -0.75
v -0.5 0.0 -0.75
v 0.5 0.0 -0.75
v 0.0 0.87 0.75
v -0.5 0.0 0.75
v 0.5 0.0 0.75

# Front cap (Z=-0.75)
f 1 3 2
# Back cap (Z=0.75)
f 4 5 6
# Side face (becomes the world "+X, upper-right" face after the engine's transform)
f 1 2 5
f 1 5 4
# Side face (becomes the world "-X, upper-left" face after the engine's transform)
f 1 6 3
f 1 4 6
# Bottom face (rests on the ground plane)
f 2 3 6
f 2 6 5
